    "lawCode": "Rpld & add Art 8 Titles I - III, §126, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6696\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to establishing assembly and\nsenate districts; and to repeal article 8 of such law relating thereto\n\nPURPOSE:\nThe purpose of this bill is to apportion the State Senate into 63\ndistricts and to establish 63 Senate districts and 150 Assembly\ndistricts.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would:\n\n-- provide metes-and-bounds descriptions of 150 Assembly districts; --\napportion the State Senate into 63 districts; -- provide metes-and-\nbounds descriptions of 63 Senate districts.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nThis bill would amend the New York State law to provide for the reappor-\ntionment of the New York State Senate and the redistricting of the New\nYork State Assembly and Senate.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis bill establishes new legislative districts for the state Senate and\nAssembly. It is based on population figures from the 2010 Federal Census\nand population figures calculated in accordance with the Prisoner Allo-\ncation Law of 2010 (N.Y. Corn L. § 71(8). The districts comply with the\nUnited States and New York State Constitutions and the requirements of\nthe Federal Voting Rights Act.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided that the provisions of\nsection four of this act shall take effect January 1, 2013.\n\n",
